22:["$","$L34",null,{"faqs":[{"question":"What is paid media (PPC), and what does a PPC agency do?","answer":"Paid media (PPC, pay-per-click) is advertising on Google, Meta/Facebook, and other platforms where you pay to appear at the top of search or in social feeds. A PPC agency or company plans, builds, and manages those campaigns — paid search, social, and SEM — including keyword and audience research, bidding, creative, landing pages, and tracking — to turn ad spend into measurable revenue."},{"question":"PPC or SEO — which should I invest in?","answer":"PPC is the fastest way to get to the top — you appear today, but traffic stops when the budget does. SEO is slower but compounds and keeps working without per-click cost. Most businesses do both: ads to capture demand now, SEO building owned visibility underneath. We run both, full-funnel."},{"question":"How much does PPC management cost?","answer":"It depends on platforms, spend, and scope. Our PPC services — Google Ads management, paid search, and Meta — are billed as a transparent flat management fee, not a percentage of your ad spend (which rewards an agency for making you spend more). You pay the ad platforms directly, so you always control and see your budget. We scope it up front, no surprises."},{"question":"Google Ads or Facebook/Meta Ads — which is right for me?","answer":"Google Ads captures high-intent demand — people already searching for what you offer. Meta (Facebook/Instagram) finds buyers by audience before they search, great for awareness and retargeting. The right mix depends on your goals and margins; most businesses benefit from both, and we'll tell you where your money works hardest."},{"question":"Do I own my ad account?","answer":"Yes — always. Many agencies hold your Google Ads or Meta account hostage so you can't leave. With us, the accounts, data, and history are yours from day one. Full transparency, no lock-in."},{"question":"How do you measure ROI?","answer":"We set up proper conversion tracking and GA4 so every dollar ties to a real outcome — leads or sales, not just clicks. We report on ROAS (return on ad spend) and cost-per-acquisition, and optimize toward profit, not vanity metrics."}],"id":"faq","title":"What teams ask before hiring for paid media.","fill":true}]
23:["$","section",null,{"data-reveal":true,"className":"border-b-hairline-soft py-20","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-mono text-label uppercase text-fg-muted [letter-spacing:var(--tracking-label)]","children":"Related services"}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"mt-4 font-display text-display-m font-bold text-fg","children":"Often paired with paid media"}],["$","ul",null,{"data-reveal-stagger":true,"className":"mt-8 flex flex-col gap-4","children":[["$","li","seo",{"children":"$L35"}],["$","li","web-development",{"children":"$L36"}],["$","li","generative-engine-optimization",{"children":"$L37"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-20 font-mono text-label uppercase text-fg-muted [letter-spacing:var(--tracking-label)]","children":"Learn more"}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"mt-4 font-display text-display-m font-bold text-fg","children":"From the blog"}],["$","$L38",null,{"posts":[{"title":"Google Ads vs Facebook Ads: which to start with?","slug":"google-ads-vs-facebook-ads","category":"Guide","excerpt":"Google Ads vs Facebook Ads comes down to intent: Google captures people already searching for what you sell, Facebook creates demand for people who aren't. Here's which to start with, what each costs, and how to choose for your business.","readMin":6,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/ppc-google-vs-meta-logos.webp","imageAlt":"Google Ads vs Meta logos, comparing Google Ads and Facebook ads for PPC"},{"title":"How to choose a PPC agency (avoid the markups)","slug":"how-to-choose-a-ppc-agency","category":"Guide","excerpt":"Learning how to choose a PPC agency comes down to three things: who owns the account, how they charge, and what they optimize for. Here's the checklist that separates ROI-focused partners from agencies billing you a markup on your own ad spend.","readMin":7,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/ppc-choose-meta.webp","imageAlt":"A PPC agency team pitching with Meta and Google Ads, illustrating how to choose a PPC agency"},{"title":"How to lower your cost per acquisition","slug":"lower-cost-per-acquisition","category":"Guide","excerpt":"A practical, operator-readable playbook to lower cost per acquisition across Google and Meta — fix tracking, kill wasted spend, tighten targeting, and improve the page after the click. No vanity metrics.","readMin":7,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/ppc-lower-cpa-sprout.webp","imageAlt":"Coins with a growing green sprout, a metaphor for lowering cost per acquisition"},{"title":"PPC management cost: what you actually pay","slug":"ppc-management-cost","category":"Guide","excerpt":"PPC management cost is the fee you pay an agency to run your paid ads — separate from the ad spend itself. Here's the real PPC management cost breakdown: percent-of-spend vs flat fee, what's included, and how to avoid paying more as you grow.","readMin":7,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/ppc-cost-meta.webp","imageAlt":"Hands with coins beside Meta and Google Ads logos, representing PPC management cost"},{"title":"SEO vs PPC: which should you invest in?","slug":"seo-vs-ppc","category":"Guide","excerpt":"SEO vs PPC isn't either/or — PPC buys traffic now, SEO compounds it for free later. Here's the real comparison: cost, speed, ROI, and which one to fund first based on where your business actually is.","readMin":5,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/redef-seo-vs-ppc-dollars.webp","imageAlt":"A growing green sprout versus US dollar bills, a metaphor for SEO vs PPC"},{"title":"What is PPC? (and what it actually costs)","slug":"what-is-ppc","category":"Guide","excerpt":"What is PPC? Pay-per-click advertising lets you buy visibility on Google and Meta and pay only when someone clicks. Here's how PPC works, what it actually costs, and how to tell if it's worth it.","readMin":6,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/ppc-what-is-explaining.webp","imageAlt":"A marketing professional explaining a concept to a colleague, illustrating what PPC is"}],"className":"mt-8"}]]}]
